        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/t/3ec8ea/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2019-03-01T07:07:23.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Noobie question on how Defend&nbsp;works. According to the rulebook (Page 18)<br>\n<br>\n\" 'Defend 2'&nbsp;means 'Whenever the Invaders may deal damage to target land or Dahan this turn, reduce the total number of damage they do by 2...Defend effects last for the entire turn.\"</p>\n<p>I initially thought that Defend&nbsp;acts as extra permanent hit points (For example, if a land with Defend 10 that turn was dealt 4 damage from invaders, the land would take no damage and have Defend 6 next turn and so on until it was dealt enough damage to get rid of it completely) But the rules&nbsp;seem&nbsp;to imply that Defend only lasts for the turn, so in the above example, you effectively have 6 Defend wasted. But then Vital Strength's power is getting Defend 3 when you make a Sacred Site; does that wear off the turn after you make the site?&nbsp;<br>\n<br>\nTl;dr. Does Defend last beyond the turn you put it on a target land?</p>",
        "post_number": 1,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:52:31.427Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
