        "raw": "<p>Noobie question on how Defend&nbsp;works. According to the rulebook (Page 18)<br />\r\n<br />\r\n\" 'Defend 2'&nbsp;means 'Whenever the Invaders may deal damage to target land or Dahan this turn, reduce the total number of damage they do by 2...Defend effects last for the entire turn.\"</p>\r\n\r\n<p>I initially thought that Defend&nbsp;acts as extra permanent hit points (For example, if a land with Defend 10 that turn was dealt 4 damage from invaders, the land would take no damage and have Defend 6 next turn and so on until it was dealt enough damage to get rid of it completely) But the rules&nbsp;seem&nbsp;to imply that Defend only lasts for the turn, so in the above example, you effectively have 6 Defend wasted. But then Vital Strength's power is getting Defend 3 when you make a Sacred Site; does that wear off the turn after you make the site?&nbsp;<br />\r\n<br />\r\nTl;dr. Does Defend last beyond the turn you put it on a target land?</p>",
